{"id":"s1.2.3","slug":"multiplying-by-25-trick","title":"Multiplying by 25 Trick","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">To multiply a number by 25, you can think of 25 as $\\frac{100}{4}$. The strategy is to divide the number by 4 and then multiply by 100 (or move the decimal two places to the right).</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For example, $84 \\times 25 = \\frac{84}{4} \\times 100 = 21 \\times 100 = 2100$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">Similarly, to divide by 25, you multiply by 4 and move the decimal two places to the left. For example, $415 \\div 25 = \\frac{415 \\times 4}{100} = \\frac{1660}{100} = 16.6$.</p>","summary":"To multiply a number by 25, you can think of 25 as .","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem involving multiplying or dividing a number (that is a multiple of 4) by 25.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $240 \\times 25$.","answer":"6000","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $25 \\times 432$.","answer":"10800","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $2.6 \\times 2.5$.","answer":"6.5","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $148 \\times 25$.","answer":"3700","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $25 \\times 33$.","answer":"825","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $64 \\div 25$.","answer":"2.56","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $25 \\times 147$.","answer":"3675","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $418 \\times 25$.","answer":"10450","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":9,"text":"Calculate $616 \\div 25$.","answer":"24.64","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":10,"text":"Calculate $2.5 \\times 40.4$.","answer":"101","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":11,"text":"Calculate $1.1 \\div 2.5$.","answer":"0.44","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":12,"text":"Calculate $3232 \\times 25$.","answer":"80800","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":13,"text